node_modules/
# Also ignore a node_modules *symlink* (worktree pattern: ln -s <main>/node_modules).
# `node_modules/` matches only directories — a symlink slips through and can be
# committed by accident (regression: a self-referencing symlink landed on staging).
node_modules
packages/*/node_modules
.claude/orchestrator-prompts/*
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/README.md
# Allow umbrella subdirs back into tracking so done.md closure markers AND
# kickoff design docs can be committed (CLAUDE.md «Umbrella closure convention»,
# #274; cross-session kickoff portability, SSOT #116). kickoff.md is a durable
# committed design doc (joins done.md as a tracked exception); state.md and the
# _plan-cache / _master-backlog-delta runtime files inside subdirs stay ignored
# via the explicit subpath ignore below.
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/*/
.claude/orchestrator-prompts/*/*
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/*/done.md
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/*/kickoff.md
# Umbrella backfill reports (e.g. umbrella-donemd-backfill/report.md) are durable
# committed audit artefacts: population enumeration + per-verdict evidence + the
# UNCLEAR table. Same durable-committed class as done.md/kickoff.md. Per-umbrella
# glob mirrors the done.md/kickoff.md exceptions.
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/*/report.md
# Calibration ledgers (arch-v2-context-pipeline ADR-5/ADR-6/ADR-8). Same durable-committed
# class as done.md/kickoff.md/report.md: pre-registered threshold + row schema + per-row
# dispatch records. Tracked so the dispatching session can append rows that reach `staging`
# for the next stage's aif container base to read (kickoff-staging-placement.md §1 shape).
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/*/calibration.md
# Stage dispatch chain for the modular-install-fullpack umbrella (S0 boundary
# blueprint + S1-S5 dispatch inputs). Same durable-committed-design-doc class as
# kickoff.md; tracked so kickoff-s0.md reaches `staging` for aif/S1 to read from
# the container base (.claude/rules/kickoff-staging-placement.md §1), and s1-s5
# stay portable across sessions/worktrees (SSOT #116). Per-umbrella glob (not the
# migration-ast per-file form) because this chain has five dispatch stages, not one.
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/modular-install-fullpack/kickoff-s*.md
# beta-delivery-ux per-stage dispatch inputs (S1-S5 + R1). Same rationale as the
# modular-install-fullpack glob above: `dispatch.ts:207` refuses a `-meta-launch`
# kickoff (a meta-plan yields no code), so each stage needs its OWN buildable
# kickoff, and it must be tracked to reach `staging` for the aif container base to
# read (.claude/rules/kickoff-staging-placement.md §1). Per-umbrella glob — this
# umbrella has six dispatch stages.
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/beta-delivery-ux/kickoff-s*.md
!.claude/orchestrator-prompts/beta-delivery-ux/kickoff-r*.md
*.log
.DS_Store
*.tgz
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Stryker mutation testing output (Wave 9.2)
packages/*/reports/

# AIF (ai-factory / aif-handoff) install scaffolding — tool-generated, per-consumer
# output, never tracked. Without these ignores, aif-handoff's branch-isolation
# dirty-worktree guard (packages/shared/src/gitIsolation.ts → assertWorkingTreeClean)
# sees the installer's own files as uncommitted work and refuses to create/switch
# task branches (BranchIsolationError "dirty_worktree"). Root-anchored to avoid
# touching the framework's own tracked .claude/skills/* entries.
/.ai-factory/*
/.ai-factory.json
# Exception: harness-model.json is the framework's OWN tracked SSOT — the neutral
# harness-config model that scripts/render-harness-config.mjs derives CC + zcode
# config from (#894). NOT installer output. The `/*` glob above keeps every OTHER
# .ai-factory/ entry (installer scaffolding) ignored so aif's dirty-worktree guard
# stays satisfied; only this one committed file is negated back in.
!/.ai-factory/harness-model.json
# Exception: the CTX Stage 3 "channel-as-data" tracked pair — the per-harness
# capability matrix (+ its ajv schema) and the honest-degradation manifest that
# scripts/render-rule-channels.mjs computes verdicts against. Same rationale as
# harness-model.json above: framework-owned SSOT data, NOT installer scaffolding.
!/.ai-factory/rule-channel-capabilities.json
!/.ai-factory/rule-channel-capabilities.schema.json
!/.ai-factory/rule-channel-degradations.json
# zcode (a CC fork) reads config from zcode.json / .zcode/ (NOT .claude/). Both are
# operator-env shims rendered by scripts/render-harness-config.mjs --write from the
# .ai-factory/harness-model.json SSOT — maintainer-env only, never shipped (a
# consumer-facing per-harness emitter is a parked fork, #894 §7). Drift-gated by
# packages/core/hooks/harness-config-drift.test.ts. Root-anchored.
/zcode.json
/.zcode/
/.codex/
/.opencode/*
!/.opencode/INSTALL.md
/.claude/agents/
/.claude/skills/aif/
/.claude/skills/aif-*/
# Exception: aif-doctor is a FRAMEWORK-AUTHORED skill (not an AIF-installed one);
# the aif-* glob above is for installer-generated consumer skills. Track it like
# the other framework skills (dispatcher, pipeline).
!/.claude/skills/aif-doctor/

# Stryker mutation-run sandbox (never commit)
packages/core/.stryker-tmp/

# Agnosticism audit — generated conformance record
tests/agnosticism/conformance-record.tsv

# rule-research-trust-tiers S2 (kickoff AC 3): a checked-in stub node_modules
# under the Tier-1 E2E fixture is deliberately tracked — the E2E test needs a
# real installed-package.json on disk without requiring `npm install` in the
# fixture dir. Negate the blanket node_modules ignores above for this one path.
!packages/core/research/fixtures/**/node_modules/
